UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 4, Week 28, Lesson 4: Unit review and check-in', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"Unit review mixes length, mass, capacity, volume, sensible units and multi-step measurement stories.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same method to a larger number or a new context, then compare two solution paths for accuracy.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nName two skills: convert 1.5 L to mL; volume of 3×4×2 cubes.\n\nFEEDBACK\nCapacity convert; volume of prism.\n\nWATCH FOR\nSkipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nComplete a twenty-four-item measurement review. Tally errors by measure type and set one goal.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one step you corrected and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Mathematics","learning_intention":"Unit review mixes length, mass, capacity, volume, sensible units and multi-step measurement stories.","lesson_number":4,"lesson_role":"Fluency and review","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: place-value chart or number line"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["MA2-NSM-02"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Complete a twenty-four-item measurement review. Tally errors by measure type and set one goal. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Sample: new numbers solved with visible working for review; key places/values named. Do not award marks for retyping the model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Sample misconception: Skipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures.. Correction uses Capacity convert; volume of prism.. Why: restores accurate review.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Skipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Solve one fresh problem that uses review with different numbers from the worked model. Show working and name the places or values that matter.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Describe one likely mistake with review, show corrected working, and say why the correction works.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Accept any mathematically valid solution that uses new numbers, shows working for review, and names places/values. Reject copied model numbers. / Accept a named misconception about review, corrected working, and a method reason. Reject vague “I was wrong” with no repair..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"This matches the taught method for review. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Skipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures","A claim that names no evidence from the lesson material","A method that skips the key step taught in this lesson","Capacity convert; volume of prism"],"question":"Name two skills: convert 1.5 L to mL; volume of 3×4×2 cubes. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"This is the misconception to avoid for review; the other choices align with the lesson method. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Careful use of measurement and explain why it matters with clear evidence","Skipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures","Unit review mixes length, mass, capacity, volume, sensible units and multi-step measurement stories","Capacity convert; volume of prism"],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when working with review?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and a named measurement and explain why it matters, not by copying the model. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Apply review to new material and name the measurement and explain why it matters used","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence","Skipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures","Name measurement and explain why it matters only, without linking it to review"],"question":"Which response best applies review with new evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Mathematics answers need labelled working tied to place value, quantity or the asked operation. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Show each place, value or step and say why that step is valid","Write only a final number with no working","Change digits to look neater without checking place value","Skipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures"],"question":"Which working best supports a correct answer for this lesson on review?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The correct statement applies the taught review method; the others break place value, units or the asked quantity. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Read 1.5 from left to right as ones only, ignoring place value","Ignore units and treat 1.5 and 3 as interchangeable","Capacity convert; volume of prism","Skipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures"],"question":"Using the method for review, which statement is true?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Disagreement is resolved by checking places, operations and the question focus, not by blending answers. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Delete units so the answers appear to match","Average the two answers without checking either","Recheck places, operations and whether the question asked for the quantity you computed","Pick the longer-looking working automatically"],"question":"If two methods disagree on a review problem with numbers such as 1.5 and 3, what should you check first?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Transfer requires new numbers with the same mathematical method and a named reason. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Use the same review method on new numbers and name the places or values that matter","Retype the worked model numbers 1.5 and 3 as the answer","Change only handwriting and keep the same numbers","Skipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures"],"question":"Solve a fresh review problem that uses different numbers from the worked model and explain one key step.?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Recognising the warned misconception protects accuracy on new problems. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Label units when comparing 1.5 with 3","Skipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures","Unit review mixes length, mass, capacity, volume, sensible units and multi-step measurement stories","Capacity convert; volume of prism"],"question":"Which error is the lesson warning against for review?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Accept any mathematically valid solution that uses new numbers, shows working for review, and names places/values. Reject copied model numbers.","question":"Solve one fresh problem that uses review with different numbers from the worked model. Show working and name the places or values that matter.","sample_answer":"Sample: new numbers solved with visible working for review; key places/values named. Do not award marks for retyping the model.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Accept a named misconception about review, corrected working, and a method reason. Reject vague “I was wrong” with no repair.","question":"Describe one likely mistake with review, show corrected working, and say why the correction works.","sample_answer":"Sample misconception: Skipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures.. Correction uses Capacity convert; volume of prism.. Why: restores accurate review.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent working and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-mat-y4-w28-l4","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA mathematics alignment using verified outcome code wording where recorded in lesson-pipeline/sources; content-point mapping remains pending.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise review.","Read the mission before you start calculating.","Keep the place or unit you are working with in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your working with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the method."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the place or distance that carries the method.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore place value or working.","Prefer accurate method over a guess that merely looks neat."],"submit":["Confirm that your working and reason are both present.","Proofread digits, places and operation signs.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact place, value or distance before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and list the key numbers.","Say what each number represents in the method.","A final answer alone is weaker than labelled working."],"teach2":["Compare a weak attempt with stronger working.","Change the value or method, not only how neat it looks.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose fresh numbers that still use the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original working and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new numbers."]},"subject":"Measurement and Space","success_criteria":["I can use review with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify measurement and explain why it matters.","I can practise convert independently on a new prompt.","I can notice check needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Unit review mixes length, mass, capacity, volume, sensible units and multi-step measurement stories. Supported working follows the actual numbers and purpose of the task. Apply the lesson idea with evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["A guess with no working","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given","Unit review mixes length, mass, capacity, volume, sensible units and multi-step measurement stories","An answer copied without understanding"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about review with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nReview path: choose unit → convert → compute → label → sense-check.\n\nTRY FIRST\nName two skills: convert 1.5 L to mL; volume of 3×4×2 cubes.\n\nFEEDBACK\nCapacity convert; volume of prism.","explain":"Unit review mixes length, mass, capacity, volume, sensible units and multi-step measurement stories.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Skipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Measurement unit review.","caption":"Tally by measure type.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Review path</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">unit → convert</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Compute</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">sense-check</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: Review path: choose unit → convert → compute → label → sense-check. Then write your own working.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.\nJuno: Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this model: Review path: choose unit → convert → compute → label → sense-check. Then write your own working."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid. Supported working follows the actual numbers and purpose of the task. Apply the lesson idea with evidence. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["A guess with no working","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given","Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid","An answer copied without understanding"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about review with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nReview path: choose unit → convert → compute → label → sense-check. Look at each number, place or distance that carries the method.\n\nTRY FIRST\nWrite the key numbers from the model and say what each one represents in the method.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe most useful working names the quantities and the reason for each step, not only the final answer.","explain":"Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Writing only the final answer without working does not show the method. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Show the working","visual":[{"alt":"Practice goal from tally.","caption":"Twenty-four items.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Goal</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">weak conversion</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Risk</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">skip sense-check</text></g></svg>"}]},{"check":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison.","options":["An answer copied without understanding","Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison","A guess with no working","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about review with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nSkipping sense-checks accepts impossible everyday measures. Here is a more productive model: Review path: choose unit → convert → compute → label → sense-check.\n\nTRY FIRST\nDescribe why the warned-against approach gives the wrong value or meaning, then write corrected working.\n\nFEEDBACK\nCapacity convert; volume of prism.","explain":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific mathematical error, then show the corrected working.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that